&lt;p&gt;The AI Platform team enables product teams across Betterment to build &lt;strong&gt;useful&lt;/strong&gt; AI-powered features quickly, enjoyably, and responsibly. As Sr Staff Engineer, you will work with a team of senior/staff engineers delivering an expanding set of AI capabilities as well as shared infrastructure, LLM evaluation frameworks, and internal libraries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will help shape and lead the technical direction of our AI product development strategy, working closely with engineering leadership. You will collaborate with product and compliance partners to ensure Betterment&#39;s AI capabilities are developed with the rigor that our customers and regulators expect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By joining us in the early days of our AI product efforts, you will have significant influence over how the organization delivers exciting features into the Betterment product across all lines of business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based out of our NYC office. Below we&#39;ve reflected the base salary range we would offer for this position. Actual salaries may vary depending on factors including but not limited to location, experience, and performance. The range listed is just one component of Betterment’s total compensation package for employees.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New York City: $230,000 - $270,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer a competitive equity package, health, dental and vision benefits, life and AD&amp;amp;D, short-term and long-term disability insurance, EAP, commuter and parking benefits FSA/HSA, and 401(k) with employer match as well as a flexible PTO policy. This job may also be eligible for variable compensation in the form of a company incentive bonus.&amp;nbsp; For jobs based out of our NYC HQ, we require in office attendance Tuesday through Thursday, weekly.&lt;/p&gt;
