&lt;li&gt;Lead high-leverage projects that expand our organization’s AI technical capabilities, where AI organically enhances existing product value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product teams to ship customer-facing AI functionality to production. Develop broad Betterment domain expertise in the process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with legal and compliance leaders to scale processes that enable teams to build AI functionality quickly and responsibly within a regulated financial services environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and grow senior engineers, sharing your experience to expand their impact and accelerate their growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong technical lead capable of establishing the strategic vision for Betterment’s AI systems while also working hands-on alongside senior and staff IC colleagues to build it into reality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in LLM systems, including prompt engineering, agentic workflows, and evaluation systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating AI features in production, ensuring quality and auditability via online and offline validation, automated monitoring, and human-in--the-loop oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating at the frontier. The ability and drive to stay current with emerging tools, techniques, and best practices within the rapidly evolving AI ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear judgment about when to use AI and when not to, maintaining a grounded, pragmatic perspective on what we should ship to production today.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record leading successful projects that affect and development workflows used by multiple teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fullstack development experience including React, GraphQL, and one or more server-side languages (Ruby, Java, TypeScript, C#, Python, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
